  "id": "social-exchange-theory",
  "term": "social exchange theory",
  "definition": "Social exchange theory views relationships as shaped by reciprocal exchanges between people, so one person’s behavior can influence another person’s attitudes and responses in return. In this study, it is used to explain how mentorship leadership may affect loyalty and craftsman spirit through those back-and-forth exchanges.",
